    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be a point on the plane which passes through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. If the plane is perpendicular to the line joining the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>23</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>11</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>11</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is equal to ________.",
